71
00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:21.539
Cole Medin: And if you come from the software engineering industry, you know what I mean by that. If you think of something like you're working in AWS, and you're setting up your IAM policies or your firewalls, like, you start with zero trust, and you build permission over time as you trust your system, and you set up the guardrails and the other things for security. And so OpenClaw is the opposite of that. There's so much power. OpenClaw literally has its own computer.

72
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:26.300
Cole Medin: And there is a lot of risk that comes with that. Like, it has computer access, it can pretty much do

